Key Diagnostic Summary for Test D:
1. WKB Tunneling Ladder (l <= 9): Eigenvalues are exponentially small (E_0 ~ 1e-43 up to E_9 ~ 2.8e-5).
   Consecutive ratios r_E(l) are massive (1e3 to 1e6), explaining why C_{2, l} is large at the tail base.
2. Barrier-Top Transition (l in {10, 11}): E_{10} ~ 0.005, E_{11} ~ 0.40, E_{12} ~ 1.31. Ratios r_E collapse.
3. Semiclassical Continuum (l >= 12): Eigenvalues are O(1) bounded (E_{12} ~ 1.31 to E_{24} ~ 3.81).
   Consecutive ratios r_E(l) stabilize close to 1 (1.07 - 1.38), and gap ratios r_Delta remain O(1).
4. This completely explains why imported continuous Sturm-Liouville / Weyl laws (E_l ~ l^2) fail for Galerkin
   truncations, while the calibrated discrete envelope bar{C}_2(N; L) remains rigorous and finite.

